1|0@woahdude^1439994185#cu89fng:MN_hydroplane$:It's because the list is based on % of total Earth land mass. The difference in land area is so small that it doesn't affect the % of total land mass to two decimal places. So when the list was created, since they are both 6.4% of the total land mass, it put China first Alphabetically. edit: and I'm guessing the list on the left is was either haphazardly taken from the list on the right without checking the numbers, or the list was created with the same function but without displaying the land mass %.
